        <mxCell id="xr7RTUpOJzw9CFKvV1Ri-49" parent="1" style="shape=process;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;backgroundOutline=1;" value="Lambda Function" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="60" width="135" x="87.5" y="1018" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="xr7RTUpOJzw9CFKvV1Ri-51" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;3)&lt;/b&gt; The Go endpoint POSTs the data to Lambda endpoint, &lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;asynchronously&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp;invoking the lambda function.&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="60" width="180" x="-150" y="520" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="xr7RTUpOJzw9CFKvV1Ri-60" edge="1" parent="1" source="xr7RTUpOJzw9CFKvV1Ri-46" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;exitX=0.5;exitY=0;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.936;entryY=1.039;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;entryPerimeter=0;" target="xr7RTUpOJzw9CFKvV1Ri-32">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
            <Array as="points">
              <mxPoint x="192" y="760" />
            </Array>
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="xr7RTUpOJzw9CFKvV1Ri-61" connectable="0" parent="xr7RTUpOJzw9CFKvV1Ri-60" style="edgeLabel;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;resizable=0;points=[];" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;4&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" x="0.2764" y="1" as="geometry">
            <mxPoint y="-50" as="offset" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="xr7RTUpOJzw9CFKvV1Ri-62" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;4)&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp;Because the lambda function is asynchronously invoked, an immediate response is returned. We will then update the job status depending on the response.&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="60" width="145" x="222.5" y="400" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="xr7RTUpOJzw9CFKvV1Ri-66" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;5A) If&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp;we receive an immediate 202 response (accepted for processing but not complete), we then mark the job&#39;s status as &quot;running&quot;&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="95" width="160" x="727.5" y="365" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="xr7RTUpOJzw9CFKvV1Ri-70" edge="1" parent="1" source="xr7RTUpOJzw9CFKvV1Ri-1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.535;entryY=0.039;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;entryPerimeter=0;" target="xr7RTUpOJzw9CFKvV1Ri-32">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
            <Array as="points">
              <mxPoint x="402" y="60" />
              <mxPoint x="140" y="60" />
            </Array>
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="xr7RTUpOJzw9CFKvV1Ri-130" connectable="0" parent="xr7RTUpOJzw9CFKvV1Ri-70" style="edgeLabel;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;resizable=0;points=[];" value="&lt;b&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;1&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" x="0.2166" y="1" as="geometry">
            <mxPoint x="-2" y="-3" as="offset" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="xr7RTUpOJzw9CFKvV1Ri-76" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;b style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;5B)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;font size=&quot;1&quot;&gt; Otherwise, we mark the job as failed, and we translate the non-202 error in a client-appropriate way and indicate that no job was created.&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="55" width="160" x="727.5" y="135" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="xr7RTUpOJzw9CFKvV1Ri-79" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;3A)&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp;A new job with status = running is created, as the lambda indicated the payload was accepted.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(0, 204, 0));&quot;&gt;End initial job creation process.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="45" width="174" x="597" y="550" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="xr7RTUpOJzw9CFKvV1Ri-80" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="²jobs should consist of the following attributes/columns:&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;id&lt;/b&gt; (auto generated UUID)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;type&lt;/b&gt; (e.g. lifecycle_generation, inundation_simulation. set on backend in insert to table)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;owner&lt;/b&gt; (who originally created the job (or called /run-lambda-process), tied to user. may not be utilized until later. passed on from frontend payload.)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;status&lt;/b&gt; (running, completed, failed. jobs are initially set to &#39;running&#39; on successful 202, as lambda auto-scales to the necessary amount of requests)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;started_at&lt;/b&gt; (timestamp that begins at creation in table)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;completed_at&lt;/b&gt; (timestamp at successful completion or error. set when lambda posts back to FEAT-API)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;input&lt;/b&gt; (original payload, JSONB. copy of frontend payload)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;result&lt;/b&gt; (JSONB data type. should only contain the successful end result. if status === failed, this will be an error message.)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;including the input and the result may satisfy records preservation requirements (unless things explicitly need to be stored in s3)&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="180" width="911" x="538.5" y="750" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="xr7RTUpOJzw9CFKvV1Ri-81" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;¹this is generic. we can call this /run-hydrograph-manipulation or whatever the name of the lambda we want to run is&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="70" width="127.5" x="218" y="300" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="xr7RTUpOJzw9CFKvV1Ri-82" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="A response is returned as part of step 2." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="32" width="225" x="40.5" y="765" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="xr7RTUpOJzw9CFKvV1Ri-86" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;b&gt;1λ)&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp;A 202 response from the Lambda endpoint to the Feat API indicates that the lambda function has been invoked and is now running &lt;b&gt;separately&lt;/b&gt; (asynchronously) from the above process. We&#39;ll assume that&#39;s happening here." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="122" width="187" x="61.5" y="809" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="xr7RTUpOJzw9CFKvV1Ri-90" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="Some things to consider:&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Mechanism to retry runs?&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="120" width="279" x="668" y="940" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="xr7RTUpOJzw9CFKvV1Ri-97" edge="1" parent="1" source="xr7RTUpOJzw9CFKvV1Ri-93" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" target="xr7RTUpOJzw9CFKvV1Ri-49">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="xr7RTUpOJzw9CFKvV1Ri-106" connectable="0" parent="xr7RTUpOJzw9CFKvV1Ri-97" style="edgeLabel;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;resizable=0;points=[];" value="&lt;b style=&quot;white-space: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;1λ&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" x="-0.201" y="1" as="geometry">
            <mxPoint as="offset" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="xr7RTUpOJzw9CFKvV1Ri-93" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;span style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(0, 204, 0));&quot;&gt;Start (Async Lambda Function Run)&lt;/span&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="20" width="205" x="52.5" y="950" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="xr7RTUpOJzw9CFKvV1Ri-102" parent="1" style="text;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" value="&lt;b style=&quot;box-shadow: none !important; caret-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(255, 255, 255); font-family: Helvetica; font-size: 12px; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: center; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;&quot;&gt;1λ)&lt;/b&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="40" width="50" x="-80" y="1200" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="xr7RTUpOJzw9CFKvV1Ri-103" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;b&gt;2λ) &lt;/b&gt;Lambda function completes, either &lt;span style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(0, 204, 0));&quot;&gt;successfully&lt;/span&gt; or early due to an &lt;span style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 0, 0));&quot;&gt;error&lt;/span&gt;. Within the Lambda, we ALWAYS call&amp;nbsp;Feat API on exit to update the Jobs table with new information. &lt;b&gt;We will need to restrict the ability to update jobs to Lambdas only. &lt;/b&gt;Simplest solution for now is a shared secret.*" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="110" width="300" x="10" y="1090" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="xr7RTUpOJzw9CFKvV1Ri-112" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;3λ)&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp;The Go db handler updates the respective job row with the information post-lambda run (i.e. status == failed || completed, result, completed_at, etc)&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="117.5" width="170" x="-370" y="342.5" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="xr7RTUpOJzw9CFKvV1Ri-117" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;3λ)&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp;A new job with status = running is created, as the lambda indicated the payload was accepted.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(0, 204, 0));&quot;&gt;End job run process.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="87.5" width="130" x="530" y="630" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="xr7RTUpOJzw9CFKvV1Ri-118" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="For the time being, the frontend can just poll (e.g. via a refresh button) to get the statuses &amp;amp; results of lambda runs." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="90" width="150" x="608.5" y="-15" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="xr7RTUpOJzw9CFKvV1Ri-119" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" value="&lt;b&gt;endpoint:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;/jobs&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="60" width="130" x="520" y="250" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="xr7RTUpOJzw9CFKvV1Ri-124" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" value="&lt;b&gt;endpoint:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;/jobs&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="60" width="130" y="390" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="xr7RTUpOJzw9CFKvV1Ri-128" edge="1" parent="1" source="xr7RTUpOJzw9CFKvV1Ri-124" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.27;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;entryPerimeter=0;" target="xr7RTUpOJzw9CFKvV1Ri-46">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="xr7RTUpOJzw9CFKvV1Ri-129" connectable="0" parent="xr7RTUpOJzw9CFKvV1Ri-128" style="edgeLabel;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;resizable=0;points=[];" value="&lt;b&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;3&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" x="-0.1861" y="-1" as="geometry">
            <mxPoint as="offset" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="xr7RTUpOJzw9CFKvV1Ri-131" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;2)&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp;We create a new job in the jobs table with status = &quot;pending&quot;, along with other relevant info from the frontend payload. We&#39;ll need to pass this job_id to the lambda in order for it to know what job to eventually update at the end of its run.&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="105" width="210.5" x="-160.25" y="265" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="xr7RTUpOJzw9CFKvV1Ri-134" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="*In cases where lambda never calls back, we can set up a cron job to mark any job with duration &amp;gt; 15 mins as failed with a custom failure message. We can flesh this out later" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="90" width="208" x="400.5" y="1175" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
